reference/
bin/
dist/
tmpbin/
# `make consumer-dryrun` leaves this binary in-tree as a side effect of
# `go build ./...` from inside the mini-module.
tools/consumer-dryrun/agent-director-consumer-dryrun
# Repo-root `go build ./...` drops the main-package binaries next to go.mod.
# These are build artifacts (not source) — installable via `make install`.
/agent-director
/agent-director-admin
/cabi
/check-doccomments
/measure-exit

# Bee hives live in the enclosing project folder, not the repo. Only the
# testplans hive (consumed by the Docker harness) stays in-tree. If a future
# `tickets/<Other>/` directory appears inside the repo it should NOT be
# committed — the hive belongs outside.
tickets/*
!tickets/testplans/
!tickets/testplans/**
# ...except the bees-generated ticket index, which is regenerated on every
# hive mutation. The other hives' indexes live outside the repo, so this is
# the only one the negation above would otherwise sweep in.
tickets/testplans/index.md

# macOS Finder cruft
.DS_Store

# Pack-gate staging dirs. These now live under $TMPDIR (b.3jn), but old
# checkouts and interrupted runs can leave pack-staging.* / pack-staging2.*
# at the repo root; ignoring them keeps them out of the docker build context
# and out of git. Belt-and-suspenders for the mid-tar vanish race.
pack-staging*/

# Tree-write lock (b.k42): skills/release-agent-director/gates/README.md "Tree-write lock".
/.tree-write.lock

# Former name of the tree-write lock (the b.2y5 "seeds-mutation" lock, renamed
# in b.k42). Nothing takes it now, but checkouts that ran the older tests or
# gates still hold the file; ignoring it keeps it out of git status, which
# preflight.worktree-clean requires to be empty.
pkg/api/apitest/.seeds-mutation.lock

# Former advisory lock of the source-of-truth gate tests. Since b.9qj nothing
# takes it (those tests run the gate in temp git repos), but checkouts that ran
# the older tests still hold the file; ignoring it keeps it out of git status,
# which preflight.worktree-clean requires to be empty.
pkg/ts-bun-client/scripts/.source-of-truth-mutation.lock

# Test stub binaries — built by `make fake-tmux` / `make ts-helper`.
test/fake-tmux/tmux

# Team coordination scratch dir dropped by multi-agent workflows.
.claude/
# ...except the checked-in policy files: the sandbox deny rules and the
# run-tests skill (b.nh2). settings.local.json and everything else under
# .claude/ stays ignored. The dir + subdir must be re-included before a
# nested negation can match (git won't descend into an excluded directory).
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
.release-work/
